  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the relevant files for the readyz/PostStartHook race investigation:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 where `start-service-ip-repair-controllers` PostStartHook is registered; generates `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` after a 1-minute timeout waiting for both repair loops to complete once.\n2. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 `NewRepairIPAddress`, the repair controller that reconciles `IPAddress` objects against allocated service ClusterIPs; this is what's failing/blocking during the mixed-version window.\n3. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go`** \u2014 the PostStartHook runner/registry; wires hook completion into a `postStartHookHealthz` check exposed as `/readyz/poststarthook/...`.\n4. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz/healthz.go`** \u2014 defines the `informer-sync` readyz checker referenced in the log line.\n5. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/namespace/lifecycle/admission.go`** \u2014 source of the generic `\"not yet ready to handle request\"` forbidden error pattern used when a resource type isn't yet established/synced.\n6. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/ipallocator.go`** \u2014 the IP allocator interface/implementation the repair controller reconciles against.\n7. **`pkg/util/async/runner.go`** \u2014 `async.NewRunner`, used by the PostStartHook to run both repair loops concurrently and gate on `wg.Wait()`.\n\nThe chain: on v1.33 nodes, `New()` in `storage_core.go` selects `NewRepairIPAddress` (when `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` is enabled) instead of the legacy bitmap-based repair. That controller depends on the `ServiceCIDRs`/`IPAddresses` informers being synced and reachable via the API. During a rolling upgrade, mixed v1.32/v1.33 apiservers behind the same LB mean the new node's repair controller can hit a peer apiserver (or its own informer cache) where the `networking.k8s.io/v1beta1` IPAddress resource isn't fully established/ready yet, producing the `forbidden: not yet ready to handle request` from the namespace-lifecycle-style admission check. Since the repair loop never completes its first successful pass, `wg.Done()` is never called, the `PostStartHook` blocks the full 1-minute timeout, then returns the `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` error \u2014 which fails the `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` readyz check and, combined with `informer-sync` not yet being ready either, keeps `/readyz` red until all nodes finish upgrading and informer caches stabilize cluster-wide.",
